From 9809c0238e4f97a9d1bc07eddada99d01e4512b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elwingh <clement_1996@hotmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 14:28:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix: trim solution to Divine + pak/resource I/O so it builds
 on Linux/.NET 8
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Narrows the fork to its stated scope (read/write/edit .pak — see README
"About this fork"): removes LSLibNative (native GR2/Granny reader,
MSVC-only), the Osiris Story/Goal parser (needs Windows-only GPLex/GPPG),
VirtualTextures tileset building, and LS/Save savegame helpers from the
build, along with the LSTools.sln entries and Divine CLI actions
(convert-model[s], build-vt) that depended on them.

Also replaces the one genuine native dependency inside the kept pak-read
path — LSLibNative's LZ4 frame decompressor, used for "solid" compressed
archives in PackageReader.cs — with the already-referenced managed
K4os.Compression.LZ4.Streams decoder, and swaps ModResources.cs's Story-only
TargetGame enum for the equivalent LSLib.LS.Enums.Game.

`dotnet build Divine/Divine.csproj -c Release` now succeeds end to end
under .NET 8 on Linux (verified in the bg3tools-dotnet distrobox
container), with only create/list/extract-package(s), convert-resource(s)
and convert-loca left as valid --action values.

Not merged to main: needs review before landing, and 19c (switching
BG3Tools' Tools/ExportTools submodule to this fork) is a separate,
not-yet-done step.
